Package: simpower
Type: Package
Title: Simulation-Based Statistical Power for Causal Designs
Version: 0.2.1
Authors@R: person(given = "Jonathan Stavnskær",
                   family = "Doucette",
                   role = c("aut", "cre"),
                   email = "jona1406@gmail.com")
Description: Computes statistical power and the minimum detectable effect (MDE)
    for four causal inference designs -- two-way fixed effects (TWFE), event
    study, instrumental variables (IV/2SLS), and regression discontinuity (RDD)
    -- directly from the user's own data. Instead of relying on closed-form
    power formulas that assume i.i.d. data, it follows the Monte-Carlo
    recombination approach of Doucette (2025): the outcome is repeatedly
    recombined to impose the empirical null, the design's own estimator and
    standard errors are computed on each recombined sample, and a growing true
    effect is injected analytically to trace the full power curve. The approach
    preserves the real features of the data (autocorrelation, clustering,
    missingness, instrument strength, running-variable shape) that determine
    power. Users can vary the number of available units, the number of treated
    units, and the set of control variables across all designs; choose the
    assumed effect shape (constant, increasing, or decreasing) for event
    studies; and vary the bandwidth for RDD.
